{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to Aaron.</b> This verse possibly took place on the very first day, when he spoke to them: ״עֶרֶב וִידַעְתֶּם״. Or it is possible that it was on the morrow, and what he said to them — ״עֶרֶב וִידַעְתֶּם״ — does not refer to the evening of that same day, but to the evening of the time when HaShem would give it to them, as it says: ״בְּתֵת ה׳״ etc., to distinguish the morning."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:41.887955877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}